WEBVTT

02:54.800 --> 02:58.303
Men are haunted by the vastness
of eternity.

02:59.555 --> 03:01.390
And so we ask ourselves...

03:02.141 --> 03:05.352
...will our actions echo
across the centuries?

03:06.228 --> 03:10.315
Will strangers hear our names
long after we're gone...

03:10.649 --> 03:12.651
...and wonder who we were...

03:12.985 --> 03:14.987
...how bravely we fought...

03:16.029 --> 03:18.031
...how fiercely we loved?

04:38.487 --> 04:39.696
Good day for the crows.

04:40.781 --> 04:45.244
I Told you yesterday
and I'll tell you again today.

04:45.410 --> 04:47.913
Remove your army from my land.

04:48.080 --> 04:49.915
I like your land.

04:50.499 --> 04:53.585
I Think we'll stay. I like your soldiers too.

04:54.336 --> 04:55.963
They fought bravely yesterday.

04:56.129 --> 04:58.465
Not well, but bravely.

04:58.715 --> 05:00.217
They won't fight for you.

05:00.425 --> 05:02.427
That's what the Messenians said.

05:02.594 --> 05:05.556
And the Arcadians and the Epeians.

05:05.722 --> 05:08.767
Now they all fight for me.

05:08.934 --> 05:11.436
You can't have the whole world,
Agamemnon.

05:11.603 --> 05:13.939
It's too big, even for you.

05:14.231 --> 05:16.775
I Don't want to watch another massacre.

05:17.109 --> 05:22.072
Let's settle this war in the old manner.
Your best fighter against my best.

05:24.741 --> 05:26.743
And if my man wins?

05:26.910 --> 05:28.912
We'll leave Thessaly for good.

05:29.454 --> 05:31.123
I'm a generous man.

05:31.290 --> 05:34.042
If mine wins,
you can keep your throne...

05:34.585 --> 05:37.170
...but Thessaly falls
under my command...

05:37.337 --> 05:40.591
...to fight with me whenever I call.

05:44.219 --> 05:46.221
Boagrius!

06:03.572 --> 06:05.073
This is my man.

06:07.910 --> 06:10.245
Achilles!

06:18.754 --> 06:21.214
Boagrius has this effect on many heroes.

06:22.674 --> 06:24.509
Careful who you insult, old king.

06:28.055 --> 06:31.099
My king, Achilles is not with the army.

06:31.266 --> 06:34.019
-Where is he?
- I sent a boy to look for him.

07:11.223 --> 07:13.308
I Was having a good dream.

07:15.811 --> 07:17.229
Very good dream.

07:18.146 --> 07:21.858
King Agamemnon sent me. He needs to--

07:22.025 --> 07:24.152
I'll speak to your king in the morning.

07:24.319 --> 07:27.239
But my lord, it is morning.

07:28.865 --> 07:31.076
They're waiting for you.

07:45.882 --> 07:48.135
Are the stories about you true?

07:49.970 --> 07:52.764
They say your mother is
an immortal goddess.

07:54.474 --> 07:56.059
They say you can't be killed.

07:56.226 --> 07:59.104
I Wouldn't be bothering
with the shield then, would 1?

07:59.271 --> 08:01.606
The Thessalonian you're fighting...

08:01.773 --> 08:06.111
...he's the biggest man I've ever seen.
I wouldn't want to fight him.

08:08.405 --> 08:11.033
That's why no one will remember
your name.

08:18.749 --> 08:22.127
Achilles! Achilles! Achilles!

08:22.294 --> 08:26.048
Achilles! Achilles! Achilles!

08:35.766 --> 08:39.269
Perhaps we should have our war tomorrow,
when you're better rested.

08:39.436 --> 08:41.980
I Should have you whipped
for your impudence!

08:44.357 --> 08:45.901
Perhaps you should fight him.

08:46.359 --> 08:48.028
Achilles.

08:48.779 --> 08:50.614
Achilles.

08:52.324 --> 08:56.161
Look at the men's faces.
You can save hundreds of them.

08:57.704 --> 09:01.041
You can end this war
with a swing of your sword.

09:02.125 --> 09:05.712
Think how many songs they'll sing
in your honor.

09:06.630 --> 09:08.840
Let them go home to their wives.

09:14.638 --> 09:19.309
Imagine a king who fights his own battles.
Wouldn't that be a sight.

09:22.521 --> 09:27.442
Of all the warlords loved by the gods,
I hate him the most.

09:28.735 --> 09:30.904
We need him, my king.

09:31.738 --> 09:33.615
For now.

10:26.334 --> 10:28.253
Is there no one else?

10:33.758 --> 10:35.510
Is there no one else?

10:40.515 --> 10:42.142
Who are you, soldier?

10:43.143 --> 10:46.104
Achilles. Son of Peleus.

10:47.022 --> 10:48.356
Achilles?

10:49.107 --> 10:50.942
I'll remember the name.

10:52.110 --> 10:55.488
The ruler of Thessaly carries this scepter.

10:57.282 --> 10:58.617
Give it to your king.

11:00.202 --> 11:01.745
He's not my king.

11:20.847 --> 11:23.391
-Brothers in arms!
-Brothers in arms!

11:23.558 --> 11:25.769
-Friendship!
-Friendship!

11:33.401 --> 11:36.738
Princes of Troy,
on our last night together...

11:37.530 --> 11:39.366
...Queen Helen and I salute you.

11:42.160 --> 11:44.496
We've had our conflicts before, it's true.

11:45.163 --> 11:48.375
We fought many battles, Sparta and Troy.
And fought well!

11:50.627 --> 11:53.004
But I have always respected your father.

11:53.171 --> 11:55.757
Priam is a good king, a good man.

11:55.924 --> 11:59.970
I Respected him as an adversary.
I respect him now as my ally.

12:01.179 --> 12:03.932
Hector, Paris, young princes, come.
Stand.

12:04.474 --> 12:05.809
Drink with me.

12:08.436 --> 12:09.771
Let us drink to peace.

12:10.605 --> 12:14.192
To peace between Troy and Sparta.

12:15.694 --> 12:19.698
May the gods keep the wolves in the hills
and the women in our beds.

12:43.847 --> 12:46.182
-For the gods.
-For the gods.

12:48.018 --> 12:50.812
Strong arm.
Thank the gods we made peace.

12:50.979 --> 12:54.524
I've seen too many of my men struck down
with this arm.

12:54.691 --> 12:55.817
Never again, I hope.

12:56.985 --> 12:59.904
Only one man wields a sword
better than you.

13:00.071 --> 13:01.072
Achilles.

13:01.239 --> 13:02.407
That madman.

13:02.574 --> 13:07.454
He would hurl a spear at Zeus himself.
If the god insulted him.

13:10.415 --> 13:14.294
See that one over there?
I picked her special for you.

13:14.627 --> 13:17.839
She's a little lioness.

13:19.215 --> 13:22.927
Thank you.
My wife waits for me in Troy.

13:24.054 --> 13:26.639
My wife waits for me right there.

13:26.806 --> 13:28.099
Wives are for breeding.

13:28.266 --> 13:32.103
You understand, for making little princes.
Come enjoy yourself tonight.

13:33.897 --> 13:36.566
You make excellent wine in Sparta.

14:26.950 --> 14:28.743
You shouldn't be here.

14:32.956 --> 14:35.333
That's what you said last night.

14:36.292 --> 14:38.461
Last night was a mistake.

14:40.797 --> 14:42.674
And the night before?

14:43.758 --> 14:46.261
I've made many mistakes this week.

15:01.860 --> 15:04.154
Do you want me to go?

15:07.949 --> 15:09.701
Yes.

15:20.503 --> 15:22.380
Where should I go?

15:23.715 --> 15:25.300
Away.

15:27.010 --> 15:28.720
Far away.

16:24.901 --> 16:27.153
I Have something for you.

16:34.702 --> 16:36.621
Pearls from the Sea of Propontis.

16:47.840 --> 16:49.551
They're beautiful.

16:51.386 --> 16:53.221
But I can't wear them.

16:54.264 --> 16:56.558
Menelaus would kill us both.

16:58.643 --> 17:00.478
Don't be afraid of him.

17:01.563 --> 17:03.731
I'm not afraid of dying.

17:06.651 --> 17:08.736
I'm afraid of tomorrow.

17:12.073 --> 17:16.160
I'm afraid of watching you sail away
and knowing you'll never come back.

17:20.873 --> 17:24.961
Before you came to Sparta, I was a ghost.

17:26.546 --> 17:29.716
I Walked, and I ate,
and I swam in the sea...

17:30.842 --> 17:33.011
...but I was just a ghost.

17:33.428 --> 17:35.179
You don't have to fear tomorrow.

17:39.684 --> 17:41.477
Come with me.

17:49.527 --> 17:52.155
Don't play with me. Don't play.

17:53.531 --> 17:56.576
If you come, we'll never be safe.

17:57.327 --> 18:00.622
Men will hunt us, the gods will curse us.

18:01.831 --> 18:03.082
But I'll love you.

18:05.376 --> 18:07.378
Till the day they burn my body...

18:08.296 --> 18:10.214
...I will love you.

18:34.781 --> 18:36.324
Tecton.

18:37.742 --> 18:40.912
Make the proper offerings to Poseidon
before we sail.

18:41.079 --> 18:43.247
We don't need any more widows in Troy.

18:43.748 --> 18:45.667
Goat or pig?

18:47.210 --> 18:49.087
Which does the sea god prefer?

18:50.213 --> 18:52.548
I'll wake the priest and ask him.

18:56.094 --> 18:57.136
Paris.

19:01.933 --> 19:05.603
We should get to bed.
We won't sleep on land again for weeks.

19:05.770 --> 19:08.398
I Have no trouble sleeping on the seas,
brother.

19:08.564 --> 19:10.566
Athena sings lullabies to me.

19:12.443 --> 19:14.779
And who sang lullabies to you tonight?

19:15.279 --> 19:16.739
Tonight?

19:18.574 --> 19:21.452
Tonight was the fisherman's wife.

19:22.286 --> 19:23.788
A lovely creature.

19:24.914 --> 19:27.375
I Hope you didn't let the fisherman
catch you.

19:28.668 --> 19:30.753
He was more concerned with the fish.

19:31.045 --> 19:33.089
You do understand why we're in Sparta.

19:33.256 --> 19:34.507
For peace.

19:34.674 --> 19:39.053
And you understand that Menelaus,
the king of Sparta, is a very powerful man.

19:39.220 --> 19:41.723
And that his brother Agamemnon,
the king of Mycenae...

19:41.889 --> 19:43.933
...commands all the Greek forces.

19:45.101 --> 19:47.562
What does this have to do
with the fisherman's wife?

19:47.729 --> 19:49.147
Paris...

19:49.313 --> 19:51.607
...you're my brother and I love you.

19:51.774 --> 19:54.277
But if you do anything
to endanger Troy...

19:54.444 --> 19:58.156
...I will rip your pretty face
from your pretty skull.

20:02.702 --> 20:04.954
Now get some sleep.

20:05.204 --> 20:07.498
We sail in the morning.

20:31.230 --> 20:35.443
A beautiful morning.
Poseidon has blessed our voyage.

20:36.027 --> 20:39.822
Sometimes the gods bless you in the
morning and curse you in the afternoon.

20:39.989 --> 20:42.950
Drop sail!

20:44.535 --> 20:46.037
Do you love me, brother?

20:47.580 --> 20:49.707
Would you protect me
against any enemy?

20:52.710 --> 20:54.921
The last time you spoke to me like this...

20:55.087 --> 20:58.424
...you were 10 years old,
and you'd just stolen Father's horse.

20:59.550 --> 21:00.802
What have you done now?

21:02.804 --> 21:04.180
I Must show you something.

21:37.964 --> 21:39.674
-Where is she?
-Who, my king?

21:40.007 --> 21:44.387
I Swear by the father of the gods,
I will gut you here if you don't tell me!

21:45.930 --> 21:47.723
My king!

21:48.516 --> 21:49.934
She left.

21:50.518 --> 21:51.769
With the Trojans.

21:56.691 --> 21:59.610
The fisherman here saw her
board their ship.

22:00.653 --> 22:02.113
The Trojans?

22:02.446 --> 22:04.615
With the young prince, Paris. She...

22:11.372 --> 22:13.541
Get my ship ready.

22:15.001 --> 22:17.128
Turn us round. Back to Sparta.

22:17.295 --> 22:18.588
High on the sail!

22:18.754 --> 22:20.298
-Wait, wait.
-You fool!

22:20.464 --> 22:22.800
-Listen to me.
-Do you know what you've done?

22:23.092 --> 22:26.470
Do you know how many years our father
worked for peace?

22:26.971 --> 22:28.890
I love her.

22:30.266 --> 22:31.976
It's all a game to you, isn't it?

22:32.143 --> 22:35.980
You roam from town to town, bedding
merchants' wives and temple mates.

22:36.147 --> 22:38.149
You think you know
something about love.

22:38.482 --> 22:42.695
What about your father's love? You spat on
him when you brought her on this ship!

22:42.862 --> 22:46.782
What about the love for your country?
You'd let Troy burn for this woman?

22:50.453 --> 22:52.705
I Won't let you start a war for her.

22:52.872 --> 22:54.373
May I speak?

22:55.541 --> 22:59.629
What you're saying is true. I've wronged
you. I've wronged our father.

22:59.795 --> 23:02.840
If you want to take Helen
back to Sparta, so be it.

23:03.674 --> 23:05.384
But I go with her.

23:06.135 --> 23:07.803
To Sparta? They'll kill you.

23:07.970 --> 23:10.306
Then I'll die fighting.

23:10.514 --> 23:14.060
Oh, and that sounds heroic to you,
doesn't it? To die fighting.

23:14.226 --> 23:17.229
-Little brother, have you ever killed a man?
-No.

23:17.396 --> 23:19.440
-Ever seen a man die in combat?
-No.

23:19.649 --> 23:23.861
I've killed men, and I've heard them dying.
And I've watched them dying.

23:24.028 --> 23:26.864
And there's nothing glorious about it.
Nothing poetic.

23:27.031 --> 23:30.284
You say you want to die for love.
You know nothing about dying.

23:30.493 --> 23:32.662
And you know nothing about love!

23:32.828 --> 23:35.706
All the same, I go with her.

23:36.207 --> 23:38.084
I Won't ask you to fight my war.

23:41.379 --> 23:43.130
You already have.

23:45.174 --> 23:46.634
To Troy!

23:46.801 --> 23:49.845
About ship! Set sail!

24:22.211 --> 24:25.631
-I Want her back.
-Well, of course you do.

24:25.798 --> 24:27.341
She's a beautiful woman.

24:27.550 --> 24:31.095
I Want her back so I can kill her
with my own two hands.

24:31.637 --> 24:34.640
I Won't rest till I've burned Troy
to the ground.

24:34.807 --> 24:36.892
I Thought you wanted peace with Troy.

24:37.435 --> 24:38.936
I Should have listened to you.

24:39.103 --> 24:41.397
Peace is for the women...

24:41.897 --> 24:43.774
...and the weak.

24:44.775 --> 24:48.279
Empires are forged by war.

24:49.947 --> 24:53.743
All my life, I've stood by your side,
fought your enemies.

24:54.452 --> 24:57.955
You're the elder, you reap the glory.
This is the way of the world.

24:58.289 --> 25:01.751
But have I ever complained?
Have I ever asked you for anything?

25:01.917 --> 25:04.670
Never. You're a man of honor.

25:05.671 --> 25:07.548
Everyone in Greece knows this.

25:08.049 --> 25:10.593
The Trojans spat on my honor.

25:11.927 --> 25:14.722
An insult to me is an insult to you.

25:15.056 --> 25:19.310
And an insult to me
is an insult to all Greeks.

25:20.686 --> 25:22.646
Will you go to war with me, brother?

25:35.117 --> 25:38.287
I Always thought my brother's wife
was a foolish woman...

25:38.454 --> 25:41.957
...but she's proved to be very useful.

25:43.751 --> 25:47.213
Nothing unifies a people
like a common enemy.

25:47.379 --> 25:49.548
The Trojans have never been conquered.

25:49.757 --> 25:51.842
Some say they can't be conquered.

25:53.344 --> 25:57.681
Old King Priam thinks he's untouchable
behind his high walls.

25:58.182 --> 26:01.143
He thinks the sun god will protect him.

26:01.352 --> 26:03.938
But the gods protect only...

26:04.855 --> 26:06.690
...the strong!

26:07.441 --> 26:09.693
If Troy falls...

26:09.985 --> 26:13.114
...I control the Aegean.

26:13.280 --> 26:15.950
Hector commands the finest army
in the east.

26:16.117 --> 26:19.328
And Troy is built to withstand
a 10-year siege.

26:19.495 --> 26:21.872
There won't be a 10-year siege.

26:22.039 --> 26:25.459
I'll attack them with the greatest force
the world has ever seen.

26:25.709 --> 26:28.921
I Want all the kings of Greece
and their armies.

26:29.547 --> 26:31.006
Send emissaries in the morning.

26:31.173 --> 26:32.424
One last thing.

26:32.591 --> 26:35.928
We need Achilles and his Myrmidons.

26:38.055 --> 26:39.557
Achilles.

26:41.934 --> 26:46.230
He can't be controlled.
He's as likely to fight us as the Trojans.

26:46.397 --> 26:49.817
We don't need to control him,
we need to unleash him.

26:50.568 --> 26:52.987
That man was born to end lives.

26:53.154 --> 26:57.575
Yes, he's a gifted killer.
But he threatens everything I've built.

26:57.825 --> 27:02.204
Before me, Greece was nothing.
I brought all the Greek kingdoms together.

27:02.371 --> 27:06.250
I Created a nation out of fire worshipers
and snake eaters!

27:06.417 --> 27:09.170
I Build the future, Nestor. Me!

27:11.255 --> 27:13.424
Achilles is the past.

27:13.591 --> 27:17.928
A man who fights for no flag.
A man loyal to no country.

27:18.095 --> 27:21.640
How many battles have we won
off the edge of his sword?

27:21.807 --> 27:25.060
This will be the greatest war
the world has ever seen.

27:25.227 --> 27:27.646
We need the greatest warrior.

27:32.610 --> 27:35.112
There's only one man he'll listen to.

27:35.946 --> 27:37.781
I'll send a ship in the morning.

27:49.668 --> 27:50.836
Greetings, brother.

27:51.003 --> 27:54.882
We were told
King Odysseus is hid in the hills.

27:55.549 --> 27:57.301
Odysseus?

27:59.553 --> 28:03.182
That old bastard drinks my wine
and never pays.

28:03.933 --> 28:07.102
You ought to respect your king, friend.

28:07.269 --> 28:08.938
Respect him?

28:09.104 --> 28:11.315
I'd like to punch him in the face.

28:11.482 --> 28:14.443
He's always pawing at my wife,
trying to tear her clothes off.

28:21.784 --> 28:25.162
I Hope Agamemnon's generals
are smarter than his emissaries.

28:30.584 --> 28:32.002
What did you say?

28:35.506 --> 28:37.716
You want me
to help you fight the Trojans.

28:44.181 --> 28:45.724
You're...

28:46.725 --> 28:48.185
Are you...?

28:52.106 --> 28:55.317
Forgive us, King Odysseus.

28:59.405 --> 29:00.823
Well...

29:01.490 --> 29:03.242
I'm gonna miss my dog.

29:03.867 --> 29:06.954
King Agamemnon has a favor
to ask of you.

29:08.914 --> 29:10.833
Of course he does.

29:36.650 --> 29:38.277
Never hesitate.

29:55.169 --> 29:57.004
Fancy swordplay.

30:00.632 --> 30:02.426
Nervous?

30:04.845 --> 30:06.847
Petrified.

30:08.265 --> 30:11.018
You told me never
to change sword hands.

30:11.602 --> 30:16.065
Yes. When you know how to use it,
you won't be taking my orders.

30:34.625 --> 30:38.462
Your reputation for hospitality
is fast becoming legend.

30:44.676 --> 30:46.762
Patroclus, my cousin.

30:47.137 --> 30:49.973
Odysseus, king of Ithaca.

30:50.349 --> 30:52.142
Patroclus.

30:53.977 --> 30:55.604
I Knew your parents well.

30:55.771 --> 30:57.398
I Miss them.

30:59.775 --> 31:02.820
Now you have this one
watching over you, eh?

31:02.986 --> 31:05.197
Learning from Achilles himself.

31:06.240 --> 31:08.200
Kings would kill for the honor.

31:08.409 --> 31:10.994
Are you here at Agamemnon's bidding?

31:13.455 --> 31:14.832
We need to talk.

31:18.836 --> 31:20.838
I Will not fight for him.

31:21.213 --> 31:23.966
I'm not asking you to fight for him.

31:24.133 --> 31:26.218
I'm asking you to fight for Greece.

31:26.510 --> 31:28.679
Have the Greeks tired of fighting
each other?

31:29.012 --> 31:31.682
-For now.
-For the Greeks!

31:32.808 --> 31:35.018
The Trojans never harmed me.

31:35.185 --> 31:37.271
They insulted Greece.

31:37.438 --> 31:41.275
They insulted a man who couldn't hold
on to his wife. Is that my business?

31:41.442 --> 31:44.069
Your business is war, my friend.

31:44.236 --> 31:47.448
Is it? Am I the whore of the battlefield?

31:48.157 --> 31:50.117
The man has no honor.

31:50.701 --> 31:52.953
I Won't be remembered
as a tyrant's mercenary.

31:53.120 --> 31:56.707
Let Achilles fight for honor.
Let Agamemnon fight for power.

31:56.874 --> 32:00.127
And let the gods decide
which man to glorify.

32:01.462 --> 32:03.380
Forget Agamemnon.

32:03.589 --> 32:05.090
Fight for me.

32:05.507 --> 32:08.927
My wife will feel much better
if she knows you're by my side.

32:09.094 --> 32:11.180
I'll feel much better.

32:11.847 --> 32:14.475
Is Ajax going to fight in Troy?

32:14.641 --> 32:18.479
They say he can fell an oak tree
with one swing of the ax.

32:20.439 --> 32:22.274
Trees don't swing back.

32:25.486 --> 32:27.988
We're sending the largest fleet
that ever sailed.

32:29.573 --> 32:31.325
A thousand ships.

32:32.451 --> 32:34.077
A thousand ships?

32:34.578 --> 32:37.206
Prince Hector. Is he as good a warrior
as they say?

32:37.581 --> 32:40.584
The best of all the Trojans.

32:40.751 --> 32:44.004
Some say he's better
than all the Greeks too.

32:45.672 --> 32:47.674
Even if your cousin doesn't come...

32:47.883 --> 32:51.428
...I hope you'll join us.
We could use a strong arm like yours.

32:52.429 --> 32:54.848
Play your tricks on me,
but not my cousin.

32:55.224 --> 32:58.936
You have your swords. I have my tricks.

32:59.394 --> 33:01.438
We play with the toys the gods give us.

33:03.273 --> 33:05.108
We sail for Troy in three days.

33:09.446 --> 33:12.449
This war will never be forgotten.

33:13.784 --> 33:16.703
Nor will the heroes who fight in it.

33:41.728 --> 33:45.232
They say the king of Ithaca
has a silver tongue.

33:46.817 --> 33:48.652
I Knew they would come for you.

33:48.819 --> 33:51.196
Long before you were born...

33:51.363 --> 33:53.490
...I knew they would come.

33:58.328 --> 34:00.872
They want you to fight in Troy.

34:07.963 --> 34:11.008
I'm making you
another seashell necklace.

34:11.800 --> 34:14.261
Like the ones I made you
when you were a boy.

34:14.428 --> 34:16.013
Do you remember?

34:23.395 --> 34:24.855
Mother...

34:26.690 --> 34:28.609
...tonight, I decide.

34:33.697 --> 34:36.199
If you stay in Larisa...

34:37.034 --> 34:38.660
...you will find peace.

34:38.827 --> 34:40.621
You will find a wonderful woman.

34:40.787 --> 34:44.541
You will have sons and daughters,
and they will have children.

34:44.708 --> 34:46.710
And they will love you.

34:47.377 --> 34:50.130
When you are gone,
they will remember you.

34:53.383 --> 34:57.387
But when your children are dead
and their children after them...

34:58.388 --> 35:00.515
...your name will be lost.

35:04.311 --> 35:05.687
If you go to Troy...

35:06.813 --> 35:09.441
...glory will be yours.

35:10.609 --> 35:15.155
They will write stories about your
victories for thousands of years.

35:16.239 --> 35:19.368
The world will remember your name.

35:21.662 --> 35:23.872
But if you go to Troy...

35:26.416 --> 35:28.794
...you will never come home.

35:30.045 --> 35:33.924
For your glory walks hand in hand
with your doom.

35:36.218 --> 35:38.595
And I shall never see you again.

35:42.349 --> 35:44.643
You know this to be true, Mother?

35:45.477 --> 35:47.479
I Know this.

38:05.242 --> 38:07.661
-My son.
-Father.

38:12.749 --> 38:14.000
Paris.

38:21.842 --> 38:23.093
Father.

38:24.427 --> 38:27.389
-This is Helen.
-Helen?

38:27.848 --> 38:29.933
Helen of Sparta?

38:32.352 --> 38:33.770
Helen of Troy.

38:40.318 --> 38:43.446
I've heard rumors of your beauty.

38:44.948 --> 38:46.616
For once...

38:47.075 --> 38:49.035
...the gossips were right.

38:52.330 --> 38:53.665
Welcome.

38:55.292 --> 38:56.626
Thank you, good king.

38:56.793 --> 38:59.170
Come, you must be tired.

39:11.850 --> 39:13.560
Look.

39:15.353 --> 39:17.147
He's grown.

39:17.647 --> 39:19.566
He is strong.

39:19.774 --> 39:21.902
He's just like his father.

39:23.028 --> 39:25.780
-Paris!
-Briseis!

39:29.784 --> 39:32.954
Beloved cousin, your beauty grows
with each new moon.

39:34.623 --> 39:35.874
Briseis.

39:38.335 --> 39:39.753
A servant of Apollo now.

39:39.920 --> 39:44.341
The young men of Troy were devastated
when Briseis chose the virgin robes.

39:44.507 --> 39:45.634
Uncle.

39:49.012 --> 39:52.766
I Thank the gods for your safe return.

39:55.060 --> 39:58.021
-For the gods.
-For the gods.

39:58.188 --> 39:59.940
For gods.

40:15.038 --> 40:16.539
Father...

40:16.706 --> 40:19.209
...I know this is the last thing we need.

40:19.376 --> 40:23.880
It is the will of the gods.
Everything is in their hands.

40:24.506 --> 40:28.969
-But I'm surprised you let him bring her.
-If I'd let him fight Menelaus for her...

40:29.135 --> 40:32.013
...you'd be burning a son's body,
not welcoming a daughter.

40:32.180 --> 40:34.933
We could send peace envoys
to Menelaus.

40:35.100 --> 40:38.228
You know Menelaus.
He'd spear their heads to his gate.

40:38.395 --> 40:40.814
What would you have me do?

40:42.357 --> 40:44.776
Put her on a ship and send her home.

40:47.904 --> 40:50.949
Women have always loved Paris,
and he has loved them back.

40:51.116 --> 40:53.034
But this is different.

40:53.201 --> 40:55.537
Something has changed in him.

40:55.704 --> 40:59.499
If we send her home to Menelaus,
he will follow her.

41:00.417 --> 41:03.378
This is my country,
and these are my countrymen.

41:03.586 --> 41:07.048
I Don't want to see them suffer
so my brother can have his prize.

41:07.924 --> 41:10.135
It's not just the Spartans
coming after her.

41:10.343 --> 41:12.595
By now, Menelaus has gone
to Agamemnon.

41:12.762 --> 41:15.598
And Agamemnon has wanted
to destroy us for years.

41:15.765 --> 41:18.143
Once we're out of the way,
he controls the seas.

41:18.643 --> 41:23.314
Enemies have been attacking us
for centuries. Our walls still stand.

41:24.065 --> 41:26.943
Father, we can't win this war.

41:27.819 --> 41:30.155
Apollo watches over us.

41:30.613 --> 41:33.867
Even Agamemnon is no match
for the gods.

41:34.034 --> 41:36.786
And how many battalions
does the sun god command?

41:36.953 --> 41:38.538
Do not mock the gods.

41:42.459 --> 41:45.962
When you were very young,
you came down with scarlet fever.

41:46.129 --> 41:49.257
Your little hand was so hot.

41:49.424 --> 41:52.677
The healer said
you would not last the night.

41:52.927 --> 41:58.808
I Went down to Apollo's temple
and I prayed until the sun came up.

41:59.017 --> 42:03.271
That walk back to the palace
was the longest of my life.

42:03.438 --> 42:07.817
But I went into your mother's room
and you were sleeping in her arms.

42:07.984 --> 42:09.736
The fever had broken.

42:10.695 --> 42:14.491
I Promised that day
to dedicate my life to the gods.

42:14.657 --> 42:16.659
I Will not break my promise.

42:16.826 --> 42:21.581
For thirty years I have worked for peace.
Thirty years.

42:21.956 --> 42:25.043
Paris is a fool sometimes, I know that.

42:25.210 --> 42:30.006
But I will fight 1000 wars
before letting him die.

42:30.882 --> 42:35.011
Forgive me, Father,
but you won't be the one fighting.

42:54.864 --> 42:56.658
They're coming for me.

42:57.700 --> 42:59.536
The wind is bringing them closer.

42:59.702 --> 43:01.371
What if we left?

43:01.538 --> 43:04.374
Tonight. Right now.

43:04.541 --> 43:08.336
What if we went down to the stables,
took two horses and left?

43:08.545 --> 43:11.005
Ride east, keep riding.

43:11.172 --> 43:13.883
-And go where?
-Away from here.

43:14.384 --> 43:17.804
I Could hunt deer, rabbit. I could feed us.

43:20.807 --> 43:23.226
But this is your home.

43:23.935 --> 43:26.354
You left your home for me.

43:30.233 --> 43:32.485
Sparta was never my home.

43:33.069 --> 43:36.406
My parents sent my there when I was 16
to marry Menelaus.

43:36.573 --> 43:38.032
But it was never my home.

43:38.199 --> 43:40.118
We'll live off the land.

43:40.285 --> 43:44.247
No more palaces for us. No more servants.
We don't need any of that.

43:44.414 --> 43:45.832
And your family?

43:45.999 --> 43:49.836
We'd be protecting my family. If we're
not here, what's the need for war?

43:50.044 --> 43:53.798
Menelaus won't give up.
He'll track us to the end of the world.

43:54.007 --> 43:57.886
He doesn't know these lands. I do.
We can lose ourselves in a day.

43:58.052 --> 43:59.929
You don't know Menelaus.

44:00.096 --> 44:02.223
You don't know his brother.

44:02.765 --> 44:06.269
They'll burn every house in Troy
to find us.

44:07.520 --> 44:10.023
They'll never believe we've left.

44:10.190 --> 44:13.943
And even if they do,
they'll burn it for spite.

44:17.155 --> 44:19.699
Then I'll make it easy for him to find me.

44:22.368 --> 44:24.996
I'll walk right up to him
and tell him you're mine.

44:34.881 --> 44:36.925
You're very young, my love.

44:39.510 --> 44:41.387
We're the same age.

44:43.723 --> 44:46.351
You're younger than I ever was.

48:26.529 --> 48:29.031
Take up your positions!

48:53.222 --> 48:56.392
Black sail. It's Achilles.

48:56.559 --> 48:57.977
What's the fool doing?

48:58.394 --> 49:02.064
He's going to take the beach of Troy
with 50 men?

49:05.359 --> 49:08.029
Row, Myrmidon, row!

49:11.240 --> 49:12.575
My lord?

49:14.243 --> 49:16.245
Should we wait for the others?

49:17.413 --> 49:20.416
-They brought us here for war.
-Yes, but Agamemnon's orders--

49:20.583 --> 49:23.085
You fight for me, Eudorus,
or Agamemnon?

49:23.252 --> 49:24.587
For you, my lord.

49:24.754 --> 49:29.175
Then fight for me. And let the servants
of Agamemnon fight for him.

49:37.725 --> 49:39.852
Make way there! Make way!

49:50.613 --> 49:53.991
Tecton, is the Apollonian Guard ready?

49:54.158 --> 49:57.411
-Waiting at the city gates.
-Good. I'll be right there.

49:58.287 --> 50:01.040
Lysander, how long
before the army is ready?

50:01.207 --> 50:04.335
Half of our men are still coming.
We have to arm them--

50:04.502 --> 50:06.003
-How long?
-Noon.

50:06.170 --> 50:07.838
Make it sooner.

50:08.005 --> 50:11.217
And Lysander, I want patrols
to scour the countryside.

50:11.384 --> 50:13.135
I Want every home
and pasture checked...

50:13.302 --> 50:15.429
...every Trojan to be
brought inside the city walls.

50:15.596 --> 50:17.515
If they can't walk, carry them.

50:32.446 --> 50:34.156
Patroclus!

50:37.159 --> 50:38.703
Put down your spear.

50:38.869 --> 50:40.955
-I'm fighting the Trojans.
-Not today.

50:41.122 --> 50:43.040
I'm ready. You taught me how to fight.

50:43.207 --> 50:47.086
And you're a good student.
But you're not a Myrmidon yet.

50:49.005 --> 50:50.506
Look at these men.

50:50.673 --> 50:54.969
They are the fiercest soldiers in all
of Greece. Each of them has bled for me.

50:55.136 --> 50:57.138
-Guard the ship.
-But this is a war.

50:57.305 --> 51:01.601
Cousin, I can't fight the Trojans if I'm
concerned for you. Guard the ship.

51:22.830 --> 51:24.540
Trojans!

51:27.376 --> 51:30.296
All my life, I've lived by a code.

51:30.796 --> 51:32.840
And the code is simple:

51:33.007 --> 51:36.510
Honor the gods, love your woman...

51:36.677 --> 51:37.928
...and defend your country.

51:40.389 --> 51:42.308
Troy is mother to us all.

51:42.933 --> 51:44.185
Fight for her!

52:03.704 --> 52:04.747
Myrmidons...

52:06.457 --> 52:08.209
...my brothers of the sword.

52:09.627 --> 52:13.047
I'd rather fight beside you
than any army of thousands.

52:13.214 --> 52:16.592
Let no man forget how menacing we are.
We are lions!

52:20.471 --> 52:25.267
Do you know what's there, waiting,
beyond that beach?

52:25.434 --> 52:28.604
Immortality! Take it! It's yours!

52:41.617 --> 52:43.077
Fight positions!

52:43.244 --> 52:45.121
Archers!

52:46.038 --> 52:47.790
Archers, draw!

52:49.709 --> 52:51.127
Draw!

53:07.727 --> 53:09.437
Keep forward!

53:28.789 --> 53:30.374
Form up!

53:30.875 --> 53:32.418
Formation!

53:33.127 --> 53:35.254
The man wants to die.

53:55.691 --> 53:57.151
On my command!

54:04.992 --> 54:06.827
Break off! Break off!

54:31.560 --> 54:34.647
Achilles! Achilles! Achilles!

54:34.814 --> 54:36.524
Achilles! Achilles!

54:36.690 --> 54:42.238
Achilles! Achilles! Achilles!

54:42.404 --> 54:45.533
Give him the battle,
we'll take the war.

54:45.699 --> 54:49.870
Give him too many battles and
the men will forget who's king.

55:03.551 --> 55:06.470
Ajax, you need to see this.

55:08.305 --> 55:09.765
Look at him...

55:09.932 --> 55:12.643
...hogging all the glory.

55:13.769 --> 55:16.814
Row, you lazy whores, row!

55:17.064 --> 55:19.900
Greeks are dying! Row!

55:48.929 --> 55:52.141
Those men down there need help. Now!
Tecton, with me.

56:04.820 --> 56:08.157
I Am Ajax, breaker of stones!

56:08.324 --> 56:11.201
Look upon me and despair!

56:11.785 --> 56:14.288
Flank! To the flank!

57:05.839 --> 57:07.091
No!

57:37.287 --> 57:39.289
Achilles! Achilles!

57:44.545 --> 57:47.756
Back to the city! Back to the city!

58:03.147 --> 58:06.817
The sun god is a patron of Troy,
our enemy.

58:08.027 --> 58:10.696
Take whatever treasure you can find.

58:17.953 --> 58:19.621
With your permission, my lord.

58:24.626 --> 58:27.546
-Speak.
-Apollo sees everything.

58:27.713 --> 58:30.507
Perhaps it is not wise to offend him.

58:54.156 --> 58:55.574
Warn the men.

58:56.742 --> 58:58.368
Wait.

01:00:49.938 --> 01:00:54.109
You are very brave or very stupid
to come after me alone.

01:00:55.944 --> 01:00:57.613
You must be Hector.

01:01:05.829 --> 01:01:07.789
Do you know who I am?

01:01:10.792 --> 01:01:12.794
These priests weren't armed.

01:01:14.796 --> 01:01:19.176
Yes. There's no honor
in cutting old men's throats.

01:01:19.676 --> 01:01:23.096
Only children and fools fight for honor.

01:01:23.263 --> 01:01:25.098
I Fight for my country.

01:01:26.975 --> 01:01:28.685
Fight me!

01:01:35.108 --> 01:01:37.653
Why kill you now, prince of Troy...

01:01:37.819 --> 01:01:39.780
...with no one here to see you fall?

01:01:52.501 --> 01:01:54.127
Why did you come here?

01:01:54.628 --> 01:01:57.172
They'll be talking about this war
for 1000 years.

01:01:58.298 --> 01:02:01.551
In 1000 years, the dust
from our bones will be gone.

01:02:01.843 --> 01:02:05.097
Yes, prince. But our names will remain.

01:02:15.732 --> 01:02:19.736
Go home, prince. Drink some wine,
make love to your wife.

01:02:20.195 --> 01:02:21.947
Tomorrow, we'll have our war.

01:02:25.242 --> 01:02:27.619
You speak of war as if it's a game.

01:02:27.786 --> 01:02:31.581
How many wives wait at Troy's gates
for husbands they'll never see again?

01:02:32.040 --> 01:02:36.837
Your brother can comfort them. I hear
he's good at charming other men's wives.

01:02:51.893 --> 01:02:53.562
My lord, you let him go?

01:02:56.732 --> 01:02:59.526
It's too early in the day for killing princes.

01:03:31.099 --> 01:03:34.227
Achilles! Achilles!

01:03:34.394 --> 01:03:40.317
Achilles! Achilles! Achilles!

01:04:14.643 --> 01:04:17.145
-Achilles.
-Ajax.

01:04:17.604 --> 01:04:22.192
You're as fearless as the gods.
I'm honored to go to war with you.

01:04:22.359 --> 01:04:23.777
As am I.

01:04:25.153 --> 01:04:27.030
If you sailed slower,
the war would be over.

01:04:27.197 --> 01:04:29.825
I'll miss the start as long as I'm here
at the end.

01:04:29.991 --> 01:04:31.993
My lord?

01:04:32.160 --> 01:04:34.371
I've got something to show you.

01:04:52.681 --> 01:04:55.725
The men found her hiding in the temple.

01:04:56.393 --> 01:04:57.811
They thought she'd...

01:04:58.812 --> 01:05:00.480
...amuse you.

01:05:11.741 --> 01:05:13.201
What's your name?

01:05:17.539 --> 01:05:19.207
Did you not hear me?

01:05:20.667 --> 01:05:22.586
You killed Apollo's priests.

01:05:22.752 --> 01:05:24.921
I've killed men in five countries,
never a priest.

01:05:25.088 --> 01:05:27.174
Then your men did.

01:05:27.591 --> 01:05:29.551
The sun god will have his vengeance.

01:05:30.218 --> 01:05:32.053
What's he waiting for?

01:05:32.220 --> 01:05:34.431
The right time to strike.

01:05:37.017 --> 01:05:40.061
His priests are dead,
and his acolyte's a captive.

01:05:41.271 --> 01:05:44.774
-I Think your god is afraid of me.
-Afraid?

01:05:45.233 --> 01:05:48.236
Apollo is master of the sun.
He fears nothing.

01:05:48.403 --> 01:05:51.239
-Where is he?
-You're nothing but a killer!

01:05:51.406 --> 01:05:54.159
You wouldn't know anything
about the gods.

01:05:56.912 --> 01:05:59.998
I Know more about the gods
than your priests.

01:06:00.665 --> 01:06:02.167
I've seen them.

01:06:08.673 --> 01:06:10.425
You're royalty, aren't you?

01:06:13.261 --> 01:06:15.597
Spent years talking down to men.

01:06:19.768 --> 01:06:21.436
You must be royalty.

01:06:23.688 --> 01:06:25.106
What's your name?

01:06:30.904 --> 01:06:33.573
Even the servants of Apollo have names.

01:06:39.454 --> 01:06:41.289
Briseis.

01:06:44.376 --> 01:06:46.378
Are you afraid, Briseis?

01:06:47.462 --> 01:06:48.964
Should I be?

01:06:52.634 --> 01:06:54.135
My lord.

01:06:56.304 --> 01:06:59.057
Agamemnon requests your presence.

01:06:59.724 --> 01:07:02.519
The kings are gathering
to celebrate the victory.

01:07:04.896 --> 01:07:06.690
You fought well today.

01:07:08.191 --> 01:07:09.818
My lord.

01:07:14.864 --> 01:07:16.908
What do you want here in Troy?

01:07:17.867 --> 01:07:19.911
You didn't come for the Spartan queen.

01:07:20.078 --> 01:07:21.830
I Want what all men want.

01:07:22.330 --> 01:07:23.999
I Just want it more.

01:07:30.422 --> 01:07:32.507
You don't need to fear me, girl.

01:07:33.383 --> 01:07:35.719
You're the only Trojan who can say that.

01:08:19.929 --> 01:08:22.349
King Triopas, my lord.

01:08:24.142 --> 01:08:27.562
You have won a great victory,
my king of kings.

01:08:28.396 --> 01:08:32.692
No one thought the Trojan beach
could be captured so easily.

01:08:33.234 --> 01:08:35.570
A beautiful gift, Triopas.

01:08:36.321 --> 01:08:41.576
You will be among the first to walk
in the streets of Troy tomorrow.

01:08:45.246 --> 01:08:49.542
My father, Neleus, had this urn made to
commemorate his victory at Cyparisseis.

01:08:49.709 --> 01:08:51.544
I Present it to you...

01:08:51.795 --> 01:08:54.589
...in honor of an even more
memorable victory.

01:08:54.839 --> 01:08:56.424
Thank you, old friend.

01:08:57.092 --> 01:09:00.929
Tomorrow, we'll eat supper
in the gardens of Troy.

01:09:09.854 --> 01:09:11.189
Leave us.

01:09:19.406 --> 01:09:23.952
War is young men dying and old men
talking. You know this.

01:09:24.119 --> 01:09:26.204
Ignore the politics.

01:09:43.638 --> 01:09:45.473
Apparently, you won some great victory.

01:09:45.640 --> 01:09:51.312
Perhaps you didn't notice. The Trojan
beach belonged to Priam in the morning.

01:09:51.479 --> 01:09:54.357
It belongs to Agamemnon
in the afternoon.

01:09:54.649 --> 01:09:56.860
Have the beach.
I didn't come here for sand.

01:09:57.026 --> 01:09:58.319
No.

01:09:58.486 --> 01:10:02.365
You came here because you want
your name to last through the ages.

01:10:04.784 --> 01:10:06.870
A great victory was won today.

01:10:08.288 --> 01:10:10.582
But that victory is not yours.

01:10:10.749 --> 01:10:13.168
Kings did not kneel to Achilles.

01:10:13.334 --> 01:10:16.129
Kings did not pay homage to Achilles.

01:10:16.296 --> 01:10:19.924
Perhaps the kings were too far behind
to see. Soldiers won the battle.

01:10:20.091 --> 01:10:22.343
History remembers kings!

01:10:22.844 --> 01:10:24.596
Not soldiers.

01:10:26.681 --> 01:10:29.267
Tomorrow, we'll batter down
the gates of Troy.

01:10:29.476 --> 01:10:32.187
I'll build monuments
on every island of Greece.

01:10:32.353 --> 01:10:35.440
I'll carve "Agamemnon" in the stone.

01:10:35.607 --> 01:10:38.151
My name will last through the ages.

01:10:38.318 --> 01:10:42.030
Your name is written in sand...

01:10:42.197 --> 01:10:44.157
...for the waves to wash away.

01:10:44.324 --> 01:10:48.828
Be careful, king of kings.
First, you need the victory.

01:10:53.708 --> 01:10:56.169
Your men sacked the temple
of Apollo, yes?

01:10:56.377 --> 01:10:58.046
You want gold? Take it.

01:10:58.213 --> 01:11:01.299
It's my gift to honor your courage.
Take what you wish.

01:11:01.466 --> 01:11:03.384
I Already have.

01:11:06.054 --> 01:11:07.305
Aphareus!

01:11:08.556 --> 01:11:09.891
Haemon!

01:11:20.109 --> 01:11:21.277
The spoils of war.

01:11:21.820 --> 01:11:25.824
No argument with you, but if you don't
release her, you'll never see home again.

01:11:26.241 --> 01:11:28.660
-Decide.
-Guards!

01:11:30.453 --> 01:11:32.038
Stop!

01:11:33.206 --> 01:11:35.166
Too many people have died today.

01:11:37.001 --> 01:11:40.004
If killing is your only talent,
that's your curse.

01:11:40.839 --> 01:11:43.383
I Don't want anyone dying for me.

01:11:51.933 --> 01:11:57.897
Mighty Achilles, silenced by a slave girl.

01:12:01.109 --> 01:12:05.405
Tonight, I'll have her give me a bath.

01:12:06.030 --> 01:12:07.740
And then...

01:12:08.199 --> 01:12:10.660
-...who knows?
-You sack of wine!

01:12:12.328 --> 01:12:16.833
Before my time is done, I will look
down on your corpse and smile.

01:13:33.868 --> 01:13:37.830
If they want a war,
we will give them a war.

01:13:38.998 --> 01:13:43.753
I Would match the best of Troy
against the best of Greece any day.

01:13:44.462 --> 01:13:48.132
The best of Greece outnumber
the best of Troy two to one.

01:13:48.299 --> 01:13:50.218
So, what do you suggest?

01:13:50.385 --> 01:13:52.011
We surrender our city?

01:13:52.220 --> 01:13:56.224
We allow the Greeks to slaughter our men?
Rape our wives?

01:13:56.391 --> 01:13:58.142
I Suggest diplomacy.

01:13:58.309 --> 01:14:00.395
The Greeks came here for one thing.

01:14:00.561 --> 01:14:04.607
Let's be honest, my friends.
Trojans are now burning on the pyre...

01:14:05.483 --> 01:14:09.570
...because of one youthful indiscretion.

01:14:10.321 --> 01:14:12.073
Glaucus.

01:14:12.573 --> 01:14:16.327
You have fought with me for 40 years.
Can we win this war?

01:14:16.494 --> 01:14:19.205
Our walls have never been breached.

01:14:19.414 --> 01:14:21.749
We have the finest archers in the world.

01:14:22.250 --> 01:14:23.876
And we have Hector...

01:14:24.043 --> 01:14:28.589
...whose men would fight
the shades of Tartarus if he commanded.

01:14:28.756 --> 01:14:31.592
Yes, we can win.

01:14:40.852 --> 01:14:43.646
I Spoke with two farmers today.

01:14:44.063 --> 01:14:48.985
They saw an eagle flying
with a serpent clutched in its talons.

01:14:49.652 --> 01:14:52.697
This is a sign from Apollo.

01:14:52.989 --> 01:14:55.116
We will win a great victory tomorrow.

01:14:55.283 --> 01:14:56.826
Bird signs.

01:14:57.035 --> 01:14:59.871
You want to plan a strategy
based on bird signs.

01:15:00.038 --> 01:15:01.581
Hector, show respect.

01:15:02.373 --> 01:15:06.794
When Archeptolemus prophesied
four years of drought we dug deeper wells.

01:15:06.961 --> 01:15:10.048
The drought came
and we had water to drink.

01:15:10.214 --> 01:15:13.092
The high priest is a servant of the gods.

01:15:13.259 --> 01:15:15.261
And I am a servant of Troy.

01:15:17.055 --> 01:15:19.974
I've always honored the gods, Father.
You know that.

01:15:20.141 --> 01:15:23.686
But today I fought a Greek
who desecrated the statue of Apollo.

01:15:23.853 --> 01:15:26.564
Apollo didn't strike the man down.

01:15:27.648 --> 01:15:30.068
The gods won't fight this war for us.

01:15:31.319 --> 01:15:33.154
There won't be a war.

01:15:38.201 --> 01:15:40.161
This is not a conflict of nations.

01:15:40.369 --> 01:15:42.622
It is a dispute between two men.

01:15:43.706 --> 01:15:46.250
I Don't want to see another Trojan die
because of me.

01:15:46.459 --> 01:15:48.169
Paris.

01:15:49.504 --> 01:15:53.007
Tomorrow morning, I will challenge
Menelaus for the right to Helen.

01:15:53.174 --> 01:15:58.930
The winner will take her home.
The loser will burn before nightfall.

01:16:11.526 --> 01:16:12.860
Does he have a chance?

01:16:23.830 --> 01:16:25.373
Father...

01:16:26.582 --> 01:16:29.252
...I'm sorry for the pain I've caused you.

01:16:30.044 --> 01:16:32.004
Do you love her?

01:16:34.674 --> 01:16:38.886
You are a great king because you love
your country so much.

01:16:39.428 --> 01:16:41.264
Every blade of grass.

01:16:42.348 --> 01:16:44.225
Every grain of sand.

01:16:44.559 --> 01:16:45.977
Every rock in the river.

01:16:47.061 --> 01:16:49.313
You love all of Troy.

01:16:52.191 --> 01:16:54.068
That is the way I love Helen.

01:16:57.488 --> 01:17:00.575
I've fought many wars in my time.

01:17:01.909 --> 01:17:05.580
Some were fought for land,
some for power, some for glory.

01:17:07.456 --> 01:17:13.129
I Suppose fighting for love makes
more sense than all the rest.

01:17:13.296 --> 01:17:16.215
But I won't be the one fighting.

01:17:19.594 --> 01:17:21.262
The sword of Troy.

01:17:21.971 --> 01:17:25.641
My father carried this sword,
and his father before him...

01:17:25.808 --> 01:17:28.436
...all the way back
to the founding of Troy.

01:17:28.603 --> 01:17:32.773
The history of our people
was written with this sword.

01:17:35.109 --> 01:17:37.278
Carry it with you tomorrow.

01:17:40.865 --> 01:17:44.202
The spirit of Troy is in that sword.

01:17:46.204 --> 01:17:49.332
So long as a Trojan carries it...

01:17:50.333 --> 01:17:52.960
...our people have a future.

01:17:57.089 --> 01:18:00.301
The man who killed Tecton
outside Apollo's temple...

01:18:01.302 --> 01:18:04.013
...I've never seen a spear
thrown like that.

01:18:05.181 --> 01:18:06.766
An impossible throw.

01:18:10.186 --> 01:18:12.480
He has no idea what's happening.

01:18:12.647 --> 01:18:13.689
Thank the gods.

01:18:15.358 --> 01:18:17.151
Don't go tomorrow.

01:18:18.152 --> 01:18:20.905
-Please don't go.
-Paris fights tomorrow, not me.

01:18:21.072 --> 01:18:26.494
Fifty thousand Greeks didn't cross the sea
to watch your brother fight. You know this.

01:18:28.829 --> 01:18:30.665
You'd make a fine general, my love.

01:18:30.831 --> 01:18:35.336
You've been fighting your whole life.
Let other men do battle this time.

01:18:35.670 --> 01:18:40.341
You know I don't want to fight.
I want to see my son grow tall.

01:18:40.508 --> 01:18:42.635
I Want to see the girls chasing after him.

01:18:43.219 --> 01:18:44.971
Just like they chased his father.

01:18:47.014 --> 01:18:49.892
He's much more handsome than I ever was.

01:18:52.520 --> 01:18:54.021
I Must see Paris.

01:18:54.188 --> 01:18:56.023
I lost...

01:18:56.732 --> 01:18:58.734
...seven brothers...

01:18:59.110 --> 01:19:01.487
...in the Spartan wars.

01:19:03.239 --> 01:19:06.033
You'd think I'd be good at losing by now.

01:19:08.911 --> 01:19:11.122
I Can't lose you.

01:19:12.540 --> 01:19:14.333
I Won't survive.

01:19:39.942 --> 01:19:41.485
Wait.

01:19:42.445 --> 01:19:43.904
Wait!

01:19:49.327 --> 01:19:50.745
Helen, what are you doing?

01:19:50.911 --> 01:19:53.039
-Let me go.
-No.

01:20:00.254 --> 01:20:02.423
I Saw them burn.

01:20:03.758 --> 01:20:06.385
I Saw them burning on the pyres.

01:20:08.637 --> 01:20:10.264
That's my fault.

01:20:11.307 --> 01:20:14.060
It is. You know it is.

01:20:15.978 --> 01:20:17.772
All those widows.

01:20:18.856 --> 01:20:21.150
I Still hear them screaming.

01:20:22.818 --> 01:20:25.988
Their husbands died because I'm here.

01:20:26.864 --> 01:20:28.574
I'm going down to the ships.

01:20:28.741 --> 01:20:30.409
No, you're not.

01:20:30.618 --> 01:20:33.621
I'm giving myself back to Menelaus.

01:20:33.954 --> 01:20:35.831
He can do what he wants.

01:20:35.998 --> 01:20:38.167
Kill me, make me his slave, I don't care.

01:20:38.334 --> 01:20:39.794
Anything is better than this.

01:20:39.960 --> 01:20:41.587
It's too late for that.

01:20:41.754 --> 01:20:44.799
Do you think Agamemnon cares
about his brother's marriage?

01:20:44.965 --> 01:20:47.385
This is about power. Not love.

01:20:47.968 --> 01:20:50.388
Paris is going to fight in the morning.

01:20:51.430 --> 01:20:54.016
-Yes.
-Menelaus will kill him.

01:20:54.183 --> 01:20:55.518
I Won't let that happen.

01:20:56.143 --> 01:20:58.145
-It's his decision.
-No.

01:20:58.479 --> 01:21:01.148
I Can't ask anyone to fight for me.

01:21:02.608 --> 01:21:04.819
I'm no longer queen of Sparta.

01:21:07.196 --> 01:21:09.448
You're a princess of Troy now...

01:21:10.825 --> 01:21:13.369
...and my brother needs you tonight.

01:21:47.153 --> 01:21:48.821
My lord.

01:21:52.867 --> 01:21:54.869
The army is marching.

01:21:56.287 --> 01:21:58.205
Let them march. We stay.

01:21:59.373 --> 01:22:00.541
But the men are ready.

01:22:00.708 --> 01:22:03.544
We stay till Agamemnon groans
to have Achilles back.

01:22:05.212 --> 01:22:06.547
As you wish.

01:22:25.065 --> 01:22:26.609
Are you ready to fight?

01:22:27.818 --> 01:22:28.819
I Am.

01:22:28.986 --> 01:22:31.405
Are you ready to kill? To take life?

01:22:41.373 --> 01:22:45.211
At night, I see their faces,
all the men I've killed.

01:22:46.337 --> 01:22:49.298
They're standing there on the far bank
of the River Styx.

01:22:52.384 --> 01:22:54.094
They're waiting for me.

01:22:56.222 --> 01:22:58.224
They say, "Welcome, brother."

01:23:05.439 --> 01:23:07.358
We men are wretched things.

01:23:12.655 --> 01:23:16.408
I Taught you how to fight,
but I never taught you why to fight.

01:23:16.867 --> 01:23:18.118
I Fight for you.

01:23:18.285 --> 01:23:20.287
Who will you fight for when I'm gone?

01:23:23.123 --> 01:23:26.335
Soldiers, they fight for kings
they've never even met.

01:23:27.336 --> 01:23:30.089
They do what they're told,
die when they're told to.

01:23:31.507 --> 01:23:32.883
Soldiers obey.

01:23:40.224 --> 01:23:43.477
Don't waste your life following
some fool's orders.

01:23:47.898 --> 01:23:49.316
Go.

01:25:14.318 --> 01:25:16.278
Are you sure you want to do this?

01:25:17.404 --> 01:25:19.114
I Started this war.

01:25:34.755 --> 01:25:36.674
Helen...

01:25:37.841 --> 01:25:39.301
...Sit with me.

01:25:48.560 --> 01:25:53.065
All my life I have prayed against this day.

01:25:54.441 --> 01:25:56.110
Yes, my king.

01:25:56.276 --> 01:25:59.279
Call me Father, dear child.

01:26:03.033 --> 01:26:05.285
Forgive me, Father...

01:26:06.537 --> 01:26:08.038
...for bringing this.

01:26:08.205 --> 01:26:11.083
I Blame you for nothing.

01:26:11.417 --> 01:26:15.295
Everything is in the hands of the gods.

01:26:15.629 --> 01:26:17.214
Besides...

01:26:17.381 --> 01:26:21.969
...how could I blame anyone
for falling in love with Paris?

01:28:33.976 --> 01:28:35.769
Prepare to halt!

01:28:35.936 --> 01:28:37.688
Prepare to halt!

01:28:38.021 --> 01:28:39.606
Halt!

01:28:58.959 --> 01:29:00.627
Move.

01:29:10.971 --> 01:29:12.472
Menelaus is a bull.

01:29:12.639 --> 01:29:17.060
He'll charge you,
but keep your distance and use your speed.

01:29:18.478 --> 01:29:19.771
Brother...

01:29:20.564 --> 01:29:22.733
...you don't have to do this.

01:29:44.129 --> 01:29:48.467
I See you're not hiding behind
your high walls. Valiant of you.

01:29:48.634 --> 01:29:51.386
Ill-advised, but valiant.

01:29:51.553 --> 01:29:55.307
You come here uninvited.
Go back to your ships and go home.

01:29:55.474 --> 01:29:57.476
We've come too far, Prince Hector.

01:29:57.643 --> 01:30:00.103
Prince? What prince?

01:30:00.270 --> 01:30:03.106
What son of a king would accept
a man's hospitality...

01:30:03.273 --> 01:30:07.611
...eat his food, drink his wine, then steal
his wife in the middle of the night?

01:30:07.778 --> 01:30:09.863
The sun was shining
when your wife left you.

01:30:11.907 --> 01:30:14.785
She's up there, watching,
isn't she? Good.

01:30:14.952 --> 01:30:17.204
I Want her to watch you die.

01:30:18.205 --> 01:30:19.539
Not yet, brother.

01:30:21.625 --> 01:30:23.418
Look around you, Hector.

01:30:23.585 --> 01:30:27.172
I Brought all the warriors of Greece
to your shores.

01:30:27.339 --> 01:30:29.341
You can still save Troy, young prince.

01:30:29.508 --> 01:30:30.968
I Have two wishes.

01:30:31.134 --> 01:30:34.471
If you grant them,
no more of your people need die.

01:30:34.680 --> 01:30:37.641
First, you must give Helen
back to my brother.

01:30:38.058 --> 01:30:41.395
Second, Troy must submit
to my command...

01:30:41.645 --> 01:30:44.272
...to fight for me whenever I call.

01:30:44.439 --> 01:30:47.484
You want me to look upon your army
and tremble?

01:30:49.778 --> 01:30:51.279
Well, I see them.

01:30:51.780 --> 01:30:56.493
I See 50,000 men brought here
to fight for one man's greed.

01:31:00.247 --> 01:31:01.748
Careful, boy.

01:31:03.041 --> 01:31:04.835
My mercy has limits.

01:31:05.002 --> 01:31:07.421
And I've seen the limits of your mercy.

01:31:07.587 --> 01:31:12.050
And I tell you now, no son of Troy
will ever submit to a foreign ruler.

01:31:12.300 --> 01:31:16.430
Then every son of Troy shall die.

01:31:19.725 --> 01:31:21.601
There is another way.

01:31:23.770 --> 01:31:27.983
I love Helen. I won't give her up
and neither will you.

01:31:28.150 --> 01:31:29.818
So let us fight our own battle.

01:31:30.068 --> 01:31:33.780
The winner takes Helen home.
And let that be the end of it.

01:31:33.947 --> 01:31:37.617
A brave offer, but not enough.

01:31:39.119 --> 01:31:40.871
Let me kill this little peacock.

01:31:41.038 --> 01:31:45.792
I Didn't come here for your pretty wife.
I came here for Troy.

01:31:45.959 --> 01:31:48.253
I Came for my honor.

01:31:48.420 --> 01:31:50.839
His every breath insults me.

01:31:51.423 --> 01:31:54.801
Let me kill him. When he's lying
in the dust, signal to attack.

01:31:54.968 --> 01:31:58.138
You'll have your city.
I'll have my revenge.

01:32:03.727 --> 01:32:05.145
So be it.

01:32:09.483 --> 01:32:13.779
I Accept your challenge. And tonight,
I'll drink to your bones.

01:32:23.413 --> 01:32:26.500
-My lord.
-Back to the line!

01:32:41.181 --> 01:32:43.475
Make him swing and miss. He'll tire.

01:32:45.185 --> 01:32:46.520
Brother...

01:32:46.686 --> 01:32:49.773
...if I fall, tell Helen-- Tell her--

01:32:49.940 --> 01:32:51.691
I Will.

01:32:51.858 --> 01:32:53.944
Don't let Menelaus hurt her. If he--

01:32:54.111 --> 01:32:57.531
You think of your sword and his sword
and nothing else.

01:34:09.186 --> 01:34:10.812
Get up.

01:34:11.229 --> 01:34:12.939
Come on.

01:34:58.235 --> 01:34:59.653
See the crows?

01:35:01.655 --> 01:35:03.782
They never tasted prince before.

01:35:38.149 --> 01:35:42.529
Is this what you left me for?!

01:35:42.696 --> 01:35:44.364
Fight!

01:35:44.698 --> 01:35:46.032
Fight me!

01:35:47.200 --> 01:35:48.410
You coward!

01:35:48.576 --> 01:35:49.869
Fight me!

01:35:50.036 --> 01:35:52.414
We have a pact! Fight!

01:35:52.956 --> 01:35:55.917
Fight him, son. Fight him.

01:35:56.084 --> 01:35:59.879
-Fight me!
-The Trojans have violated the agreement!

01:36:00.046 --> 01:36:02.590
Prepare for battle!

01:36:04.342 --> 01:36:05.677
This is not honor!

01:36:05.927 --> 01:36:08.388
This is not worthy of royalty!

01:36:08.805 --> 01:36:11.933
If he doesn't fight, Troy is doomed.

01:36:12.851 --> 01:36:14.060
Paris.

01:36:15.562 --> 01:36:17.522
No. No.

01:36:18.273 --> 01:36:19.566
The fight is over.

01:36:19.733 --> 01:36:21.901
The fight is not over.

01:36:22.068 --> 01:36:23.778
Stand back, Prince Hector.

01:36:23.945 --> 01:36:26.614
I'll kill him at your feet. I don't care.

01:36:26.781 --> 01:36:28.074
He is my brother.

01:37:23.671 --> 01:37:25.423
Paris!

01:37:34.516 --> 01:37:36.226
Go! Go!

01:37:43.066 --> 01:37:44.901
Get inside, Paris!

01:37:45.485 --> 01:37:46.778
Archers!

01:37:50.198 --> 01:37:53.410
-Our men are too close to the walls.
-Pull back.

01:37:53.576 --> 01:37:55.286
Pull back, you fool!

01:37:55.537 --> 01:37:56.788
For Troy!

01:37:56.955 --> 01:37:58.081
For Troy!

01:38:24.607 --> 01:38:26.776
-Now!
-Loose!

01:38:58.391 --> 01:38:59.809
Get them in line!

01:39:06.232 --> 01:39:09.194
Get the men back into lines!

01:39:09.360 --> 01:39:11.738
Front line, push!

01:40:21.099 --> 01:40:23.935
So you're the best of the Trojans.

01:41:39.302 --> 01:41:40.803
Forward.

01:41:40.970 --> 01:41:42.221
Forward!

01:41:58.655 --> 01:41:59.947
Forward!

01:42:14.879 --> 01:42:17.256
Apollonians! Now!

01:42:31.229 --> 01:42:32.563
Prince Hector!

01:42:40.738 --> 01:42:42.073
We need to retreat!

01:42:43.032 --> 01:42:45.243
My army's never lost a battle yet!

01:42:45.410 --> 01:42:47.912
You won't have an army
if you don't fall back!

01:42:56.295 --> 01:42:58.339
Back to the ships!

01:42:58.506 --> 01:43:00.216
-Back to the ships!
-Retreat!

01:43:00.383 --> 01:43:01.384
-Back!
-Retreat!

01:43:01.551 --> 01:43:03.344
Go back!

01:43:11.519 --> 01:43:13.354
Back. Back to the ships!

01:44:19.962 --> 01:44:21.547
Fall back!

01:44:21.923 --> 01:44:24.425
-Men, fall back!
-Halt!

01:44:31.682 --> 01:44:33.100
Halt!

01:44:33.309 --> 01:44:34.769
But we have them on the run!

01:44:35.019 --> 01:44:37.230
We're in range of their archers.

01:44:37.396 --> 01:44:39.273
Have our men gather our fallen.

01:44:39.440 --> 01:44:42.401
Send an emissary to them.
They can collect their dead.

01:44:42.568 --> 01:44:45.071
Would they have done the same for us?

01:44:48.032 --> 01:44:49.617
Go! Back!

01:44:50.493 --> 01:44:52.203
Fall back into line!

01:45:56.893 --> 01:45:59.103
Before I leave...

01:45:59.353 --> 01:46:02.899
...I will burn their city to the ground.

01:46:03.065 --> 01:46:06.903
Brother, I promise you that.

01:46:35.389 --> 01:46:40.645
They're laughing at me in Troy.
Drunk with victory!

01:46:41.020 --> 01:46:44.023
They think I'll sail home at first light.

01:46:44.190 --> 01:46:45.524
Maybe we should.

01:46:45.691 --> 01:46:48.027
Flee? Like a whipped dog?

01:46:48.235 --> 01:46:51.864
The men believe we came here
for Menelaus' wife.

01:46:53.115 --> 01:46:54.784
Won't be needing her anymore.

01:46:54.992 --> 01:46:58.120
My brother's blood still wets the sand,
and you insult him!

01:46:58.329 --> 01:47:00.957
It's no insult to say a dead man is dead.

01:47:01.165 --> 01:47:04.251
If we leave now, we lose all credibility.

01:47:04.460 --> 01:47:08.881
The Trojans can beat us so easily.
How long before the Hittites invade?

01:47:09.048 --> 01:47:13.552
If we stay, we stay here
for the right reasons.

01:47:13.719 --> 01:47:15.888
To protect Greece, not your pride.

01:47:16.055 --> 01:47:18.808
Your private battle with Achilles
is destroying us.

01:47:18.975 --> 01:47:20.226
Achilles is one man.

01:47:20.393 --> 01:47:22.812
Hector is one man.

01:47:23.396 --> 01:47:24.814
Look what he did to us today.

01:47:25.022 --> 01:47:28.985
Hector fights for his country!
Achilles fights only for himself!

01:47:29.151 --> 01:47:33.906
I Don't care about the man's allegiance.
I care about his ability to win battles.

01:47:34.156 --> 01:47:35.700
He's right.

01:47:35.866 --> 01:47:37.326
The men's morale is weak.

01:47:37.493 --> 01:47:40.621
Weak? They're ready to swim home.

01:47:40.788 --> 01:47:45.710
Even if I could make peace with Achilles,
the man won't listen to me!

01:47:46.585 --> 01:47:50.047
He's as likely to spear me
as to speak to me!

01:47:51.590 --> 01:47:53.050
I'll talk to him.

01:47:53.634 --> 01:47:55.052
He'll want the girl back.

01:47:55.594 --> 01:47:56.929
He can have that damn girl.

01:48:00.766 --> 01:48:01.976
I Haven't touched her.

01:48:02.935 --> 01:48:04.228
Where is she?

01:48:05.771 --> 01:48:07.440
I Gave her to the men.

01:48:09.442 --> 01:48:14.113
They need some amusement after today.

01:48:17.950 --> 01:48:20.244
Come on, give the bitch to me!

01:48:20.870 --> 01:48:22.246
Who's first?

01:48:22.997 --> 01:48:24.540
Trojan whore!

01:48:24.707 --> 01:48:26.625
What's this? A virgin's robe?

01:48:26.959 --> 01:48:29.962
-You won't be needing that for much longer!
-Hold her.

01:48:34.967 --> 01:48:37.845
Come on. Come on. Hold her down.

01:49:11.253 --> 01:49:13.089
Are you hurt?

01:49:19.220 --> 01:49:21.514
I Watched you fight them.
You have courage.

01:49:21.680 --> 01:49:26.185
To fight back when people attack me?
Dog has that kind of courage.

01:49:49.542 --> 01:49:51.043
Eat.

01:49:59.677 --> 01:50:01.720
I've known men like you my whole life.

01:50:03.430 --> 01:50:04.557
No, you haven't.

01:50:04.723 --> 01:50:07.059
You think you're so different
from 1000 others?

01:50:07.935 --> 01:50:11.814
Soldiers understand nothing but war.
Peace confuses them.

01:50:12.064 --> 01:50:14.400
-And you hate these soldiers.
-I pity them.

01:50:15.359 --> 01:50:18.070
Trojan soldiers died trying to protect you.

01:50:18.571 --> 01:50:21.282
Perhaps they deserve more than your pity.

01:50:24.243 --> 01:50:25.870
Why did you choose this life?

01:50:26.287 --> 01:50:28.581
-What life?
-To be a great warrior.

01:50:31.083 --> 01:50:34.837
I Chose nothing. I was born,
and this is what I am.

01:50:36.380 --> 01:50:39.466
And you? Why did you choose
to love a god?

01:50:40.426 --> 01:50:43.429
I Think you'll find the romance one-sided.

01:50:46.015 --> 01:50:47.600
Do you enjoy provoking me?

01:50:49.560 --> 01:50:51.604
You've dedicated your life to the gods.

01:50:51.770 --> 01:50:55.441
Zeus, god of thunder. Athena,
goddess of wisdom. You serve them.

01:50:55.608 --> 01:50:58.110
-Yes, of course.
-And Ares, god of war?

01:50:58.277 --> 01:51:01.280
Who blankets his bed with the skin
of men he's killed?

01:51:03.032 --> 01:51:05.868
All the gods are to be feared
and respected.

01:51:17.129 --> 01:51:18.714
I'll tell you a secret...

01:51:19.298 --> 01:51:21.967
...something they don't teach you
in your temple.

01:51:32.478 --> 01:51:34.855
The gods envy us.

01:51:36.565 --> 01:51:38.651
They envy us because we're mortal.

01:51:40.194 --> 01:51:43.030
Because any moment might be our last.

01:51:43.322 --> 01:51:46.617
Everything's more beautiful
because we're doomed.

01:51:47.826 --> 01:51:50.788
You will never be lovelier
than you are now.

01:51:55.084 --> 01:51:56.835
We will never be here again.

01:52:07.596 --> 01:52:09.598
I Thought you were a dumb brute.

01:52:13.185 --> 01:52:15.187
I Could have forgiven a dumb brute.

01:52:39.545 --> 01:52:40.754
Do it.

01:52:47.303 --> 01:52:48.846
Nothing is easier.

01:52:49.013 --> 01:52:50.222
Aren't you afraid?

01:52:52.516 --> 01:52:57.104
Everyone dies. Today or 50 years
from now. What does it matter?

01:53:01.900 --> 01:53:03.694
Do it.

01:53:05.279 --> 01:53:07.448
You'll kill more men if I don't kill you.

01:53:07.614 --> 01:53:09.241
Many.

01:54:44.169 --> 01:54:45.671
My lord, there's--

01:55:00.519 --> 01:55:04.273
Tell the men to start loading the ship.
We're going home.

01:55:08.235 --> 01:55:10.028
Gather the stores.

01:55:10.195 --> 01:55:12.030
Prepare the ship.

01:55:13.031 --> 01:55:14.700
Prepare the ship.

01:55:14.992 --> 01:55:17.411
Agamemnon is a proud man.

01:55:18.495 --> 01:55:20.873
But he knows when he's made a mistake.

01:55:21.039 --> 01:55:23.292
The man sends you
to make his apologies?

01:55:25.419 --> 01:55:28.172
What are you doing enthralled
to that pig of a king?

01:55:29.173 --> 01:55:31.425
The world seems simple to you,
my friend...

01:55:31.592 --> 01:55:35.095
...but when you're a king,
very few choices are simple.

01:55:37.097 --> 01:55:39.933
Ithaca cannot afford an enemy
like Agamemnon.

01:55:40.100 --> 01:55:41.768
Are we supposed to fear him?

01:55:41.935 --> 01:55:46.815
You don't fear anyone.
That's your problem. Fear is useful.

01:55:50.027 --> 01:55:51.487
We need you back.

01:55:51.737 --> 01:55:53.489
Greece needs you.

01:55:54.406 --> 01:55:57.159
Greece got along fine before I was born.

01:55:57.326 --> 01:55:59.578
Greece will be Greece long after I'm dead.

01:55:59.745 --> 01:56:01.788
I'm not talking about the land.

01:56:01.955 --> 01:56:04.208
The men need you.

01:56:07.669 --> 01:56:09.254
Stay, Achilles.

01:56:10.255 --> 01:56:11.798
You were born for this war.

01:56:15.719 --> 01:56:17.304
Things are less simple today.

01:56:19.306 --> 01:56:23.602
Women have a way
of complicating things.

01:56:27.314 --> 01:56:30.609
Of all the kings of Greece,
I respect you the most.

01:56:30.901 --> 01:56:32.945
But in this war, you're a servant.

01:56:33.111 --> 01:56:36.281
Sometimes you have to serve
in order to lead.

01:56:37.908 --> 01:56:40.786
I Hope you understand that one day.

01:56:45.999 --> 01:56:47.251
We're going home?

01:56:51.797 --> 01:56:53.048
We sail in the morning.

01:56:53.340 --> 01:56:56.802
Greeks are being slaughtered.
We can't just sail away.

01:56:56.969 --> 01:57:00.806
If it's fighting you still long for,
there will always be another war.

01:57:00.973 --> 01:57:02.391
These are our countrymen.

01:57:02.975 --> 01:57:06.144
I Ate, laughed, mourned with these men
while you hid in your tent.

01:57:07.229 --> 01:57:10.232
You betray all of Greece
just to see Agamemnon fall.

01:57:14.444 --> 01:57:16.280
Someone has to lose.

01:57:17.364 --> 01:57:21.451
In all my years to come,
may my heart never turn as black as yours!

01:57:21.743 --> 01:57:23.996
We sail in the morning!

01:57:29.918 --> 01:57:32.337
The omens are gathering.

01:57:32.504 --> 01:57:34.339
The directive is clear.

01:57:34.506 --> 01:57:36.758
Fight for your country,
that's the only directive.

01:57:36.925 --> 01:57:41.847
Last time the high priest spoke to us,
he prophesied a great victory for Troy.

01:57:42.014 --> 01:57:45.767
We won a great victory. Let him speak.

01:57:46.393 --> 01:57:48.854
What course of action
do you recommend?

01:57:49.146 --> 01:57:51.523
The gods favor our cause.

01:57:51.690 --> 01:57:54.901
Now is the time to destroy
the Greek army.

01:57:56.528 --> 01:57:57.821
Glaucus?

01:57:58.697 --> 01:58:00.991
Their morale is battered.

01:58:01.158 --> 01:58:04.369
Hit them now. Hit them hard.

01:58:04.536 --> 01:58:06.371
And they will run.

01:58:09.207 --> 01:58:12.836
I Must admit,
I overestimated the Greeks.

01:58:13.545 --> 01:58:16.256
They lack discipline and courage.

01:58:23.388 --> 01:58:27.684
The Myrmidons didn't fight yesterday. There
must be dissension among the Greeks.

01:58:27.851 --> 01:58:30.479
But if we attack their ships,
we will unify them.

01:58:31.229 --> 01:58:33.231
If they decide to attack us, let them.

01:58:33.398 --> 01:58:36.318
Our walls can't be breached.
We'll beat them back again.

01:58:40.447 --> 01:58:42.949
Yesterday, the Greeks underestimated us.

01:58:43.909 --> 01:58:46.078
We should not return the favor.

01:58:59.841 --> 01:59:02.552
You're confident about the meaning
of these omens?

01:59:02.719 --> 01:59:06.390
The desecration of his temple
angers Apollo.

01:59:06.890 --> 01:59:09.851
The gods have cursed the Greeks.

01:59:10.352 --> 01:59:14.147
Two of their kings
have already gone down to the dust.

01:59:19.277 --> 01:59:22.114
Prepare the army. We attack at daybreak.

01:59:22.280 --> 01:59:23.782
Father.

01:59:24.783 --> 01:59:26.743
We're making a mistake.

01:59:29.246 --> 01:59:30.539
Prepare the army.

01:59:48.598 --> 01:59:50.183
Come on.

02:00:17.836 --> 02:00:19.963
Am I still your captive?

02:00:22.841 --> 02:00:24.384
You're my guest.

02:00:27.012 --> 02:00:30.140
In Troy, guests can leave
whenever they want.

02:00:30.307 --> 02:00:31.975
You should leave, then.

02:00:38.899 --> 02:00:40.942
Would you leave this all behind?

02:00:45.363 --> 02:00:47.032
Would you leave Troy?

02:03:47.545 --> 02:03:49.381
Hold those barricades!

02:04:10.235 --> 02:04:12.195
Archers to the rear.

02:04:21.579 --> 02:04:23.748
Achilles.

02:04:46.896 --> 02:04:48.732
Achilles.

02:04:51.609 --> 02:04:53.236
Now!

02:05:02.370 --> 02:05:03.788
Forward!

02:07:58.171 --> 02:07:59.797
Enough for one day.

02:08:01.966 --> 02:08:03.218
Yes.

02:08:04.719 --> 02:08:06.221
Back to the ships!

02:08:06.387 --> 02:08:08.806
Back to the ships!

02:08:10.642 --> 02:08:12.352
It was his cousin.

02:08:16.731 --> 02:08:18.316
To Troy!

02:08:19.234 --> 02:08:21.402
Back to the city!

02:08:22.320 --> 02:08:23.696
To Troy!

02:08:25.823 --> 02:08:27.992
We were going to sail home today.

02:08:30.828 --> 02:08:33.498
I Don't think anyone's sailing home now.

02:08:54.227 --> 02:08:55.687
Achilles.

02:09:11.202 --> 02:09:13.037
You violated my command.

02:09:13.830 --> 02:09:17.125
No, my lord. There was a mistake.

02:09:18.042 --> 02:09:20.586
I Ordered the Myrmidons to stand down.

02:09:20.878 --> 02:09:23.006
You led them into combat.

02:09:27.885 --> 02:09:31.764
I Didn't lead them, my lord.
We thought you did.

02:09:39.522 --> 02:09:40.773
Where's Patroclus?

02:09:43.735 --> 02:09:45.445
Patroclus!

02:09:45.903 --> 02:09:48.197
We thought he was you, my lord.

02:09:50.658 --> 02:09:56.414
He wore your armor, your shield,
your greaves, your helmet.

02:09:57.332 --> 02:09:59.125
He even moved like you.

02:09:59.917 --> 02:10:02.003
Where is he?

02:10:05.798 --> 02:10:07.675
-Where?
-He's dead, my lord.

02:10:08.760 --> 02:10:10.261
Hector cut his throat.

02:10:21.105 --> 02:10:23.524
Don't. Don't.

02:10:56.307 --> 02:10:58.059
Where are you taking me?

02:11:03.856 --> 02:11:05.817
Do you remember how to get here?

02:11:06.401 --> 02:11:08.027
Yes.

02:11:15.576 --> 02:11:18.621
The next time you come here,
follow the tunnel.

02:11:18.788 --> 02:11:21.874
There are no turns, so you can't get lost.
Just keep walking.

02:11:22.041 --> 02:11:23.459
Why?

02:11:23.960 --> 02:11:26.462
When you get to the end,
you'll be by the river.

02:11:26.629 --> 02:11:29.048
Follow the river until you get
to Mount Ida.

02:11:29.882 --> 02:11:32.260
The Greeks won't go that far inland.

02:11:33.052 --> 02:11:34.679
Hector.

02:11:35.388 --> 02:11:37.056
Why are you telling me this?

02:11:42.645 --> 02:11:44.105
-If I die--
-No.

02:11:44.272 --> 02:11:47.525
If I die, I don't know how long
the city will stand.

02:11:47.942 --> 02:11:49.110
Don't say that.

02:11:49.277 --> 02:11:51.529
If the Greeks get inside the walls,
it's over.

02:11:52.238 --> 02:11:55.658
They'll kill all the men, throw
the babies from the city walls.

02:11:55.825 --> 02:11:58.202
-Please.
-The women, they'll take as slaves.

02:11:58.369 --> 02:12:01.038
That, for you, will be worse than dying.

02:12:01.289 --> 02:12:04.000
Why are you saying such things?

02:12:06.878 --> 02:12:08.838
Because I want you to be ready.

02:12:11.215 --> 02:12:15.052
I Want you to get our boy,
and I want you to bring him here.

02:12:16.387 --> 02:12:20.892
You save as many people as you can,
but you get here. And you run.

02:12:22.560 --> 02:12:23.769
Do you understand?

02:12:31.110 --> 02:12:32.862
I Killed a boy today.

02:12:34.780 --> 02:12:36.449
And he was young.

02:12:37.617 --> 02:12:39.452
He was much too young.

02:13:14.612 --> 02:13:17.448
That boy has just saved this war for us.

02:15:05.097 --> 02:15:07.266
-Eudorus.
-My lord.

02:15:07.433 --> 02:15:09.226
I Need my armor.

02:16:10.121 --> 02:16:11.455
No.

02:16:12.998 --> 02:16:14.333
Don't go!

02:16:15.209 --> 02:16:17.128
Rope!

02:16:17.294 --> 02:16:19.630
Hector's my cousin. He's a good man.

02:16:20.214 --> 02:16:23.008
Don't fight him. Please don't fight him.

02:16:23.426 --> 02:16:25.344
Please.

02:17:41.879 --> 02:17:43.214
No.

02:18:09.114 --> 02:18:11.116
Hector!

02:18:17.331 --> 02:18:19.041
Hector!

02:18:26.966 --> 02:18:28.926
Hector!

02:18:33.931 --> 02:18:35.432
Hector!

02:18:39.353 --> 02:18:41.313
Father...

02:18:41.480 --> 02:18:43.858
...forgive me for any offenses.

02:18:45.734 --> 02:18:47.987
I've served you as best as I could.

02:18:48.571 --> 02:18:50.239
Hector!

02:18:54.493 --> 02:18:56.912
May the gods be with you.

02:19:01.292 --> 02:19:02.501
Hector.

02:19:05.296 --> 02:19:08.632
No father ever had a better son.

02:19:15.306 --> 02:19:16.891
Hector!

02:19:18.767 --> 02:19:20.394
Apollo guard you, my prince.

02:19:27.651 --> 02:19:29.069
You're the best man I know.

02:19:35.326 --> 02:19:37.161
You're a prince of Troy.

02:19:37.953 --> 02:19:39.496
I Know you'll make me proud.

02:19:47.296 --> 02:19:49.965
Hector!

02:20:06.982 --> 02:20:09.068
Remember what I told you.

02:20:09.860 --> 02:20:12.863
You don't have to go. You don't.

02:20:13.155 --> 02:20:14.949
You remember what I told you.

02:20:33.300 --> 02:20:35.719
Hector!

02:20:51.235 --> 02:20:53.821
Hector!

02:22:07.811 --> 02:22:10.481
I've seen this moment in my dreams.

02:22:12.649 --> 02:22:14.026
I'll make a pact with you.

02:22:14.985 --> 02:22:17.029
With the gods as our witnesses...

02:22:17.196 --> 02:22:21.909
...let us pledge that the winner will allow
the loser all the proper funeral rituals.

02:22:22.076 --> 02:22:25.079
There are no pacts
between lions and men.

02:22:33.087 --> 02:22:35.380
Now you know who you're fighting.

02:22:43.889 --> 02:22:46.725
I Thought it was you
I was fighting yesterday.

02:22:47.059 --> 02:22:51.063
And I wish it had been you. But I gave
the dead boy the honor he deserved.

02:22:51.230 --> 02:22:53.232
You gave him the honor of your sword.

02:22:54.191 --> 02:22:57.111
You won't have eyes tonight.
You won't have ears or a tongue.

02:22:57.277 --> 02:23:01.490
You'll wander the underworld, blind, deaf,
and dumb, and all the dead will know:

02:23:01.657 --> 02:23:05.369
This is Hector, the fool who thought
he killed Achilles.

02:25:03.445 --> 02:25:04.738
Get up, prince of Troy.

02:25:07.366 --> 02:25:10.327
Get up. I won't let a stone take my glory.

02:28:43.165 --> 02:28:45.041
You lost your cousin.

02:28:46.877 --> 02:28:48.712
Now you've taken mine.

02:28:52.174 --> 02:28:53.758
When does it end?

02:28:55.802 --> 02:28:57.345
It never ends.

02:29:57.280 --> 02:29:58.823
Who are you?

02:29:58.990 --> 02:30:04.871
I Have endured what no one
on earth has endured before.

02:30:05.539 --> 02:30:10.835
I Kissed the hands of the man
who killed my son.

02:30:17.968 --> 02:30:19.636
Priam?

02:30:21.179 --> 02:30:22.556
How did you get in here?

02:30:22.722 --> 02:30:26.685
I Know my own country better
than the Greeks, I think.

02:30:31.439 --> 02:30:33.858
You're a brave man.

02:30:36.653 --> 02:30:39.823
I Could have your head on a spit
in the blink of an eye.

02:30:40.198 --> 02:30:43.994
Do you really think death
frightens me now?

02:30:45.745 --> 02:30:48.331
I Watched my eldest son die...

02:30:48.498 --> 02:30:52.377
...watched you drag his body
behind your chariot.

02:30:55.589 --> 02:30:57.757
Give him back to me.

02:30:58.842 --> 02:31:03.346
He deserves the honor of a proper burial.
You know that.

02:31:04.306 --> 02:31:06.516
Give him to me.

02:31:07.434 --> 02:31:09.144
He killed my cousin.

02:31:09.311 --> 02:31:11.271
He thought it was you.

02:31:13.857 --> 02:31:16.568
How many cousins have you killed?

02:31:18.111 --> 02:31:22.032
How many sons and fathers
and brothers and husbands?

02:31:22.240 --> 02:31:24.826
How many, brave Achilles?

02:31:29.706 --> 02:31:31.833
I Knew your father.

02:31:32.959 --> 02:31:35.253
He died before his time.

02:31:36.546 --> 02:31:41.718
But he was lucky not to live long enough
to see his son fall.

02:31:46.640 --> 02:31:49.309
You have taken everything from me.

02:31:51.394 --> 02:31:53.229
My eldest son...

02:31:53.855 --> 02:31:55.649
...heir to my throne...

02:31:56.066 --> 02:31:58.693
...defender of my kingdom.

02:32:00.070 --> 02:32:04.741
I Cannot change what happened.
It is the will of the gods.

02:32:06.034 --> 02:32:09.371
But give me this small mercy.

02:32:11.706 --> 02:32:15.835
I loved my boy from the moment
he opened his eyes...

02:32:16.002 --> 02:32:18.838
...till the moment you closed them.

02:32:21.257 --> 02:32:24.260
Let me wash his body.

02:32:25.887 --> 02:32:29.099
Let me say the prayers.

02:32:30.392 --> 02:32:35.438
Let me place two coins on his eyes
for the boatman.

02:32:40.151 --> 02:32:42.404
If I let you walk out of here...

02:32:44.698 --> 02:32:46.616
...if I let you take him...

02:32:49.285 --> 02:32:51.329
...it doesn't change anything.

02:32:52.914 --> 02:32:55.583
You're still my enemy in the morning.

02:32:56.710 --> 02:32:59.754
You're still my enemy tonight.

02:33:00.797 --> 02:33:04.384
But even enemies can show respect.

02:33:24.070 --> 02:33:25.488
I Admire your courage.

02:33:33.204 --> 02:33:34.998
Meet me outside in a moment.

02:34:21.044 --> 02:34:22.754
We'll meet again soon, my brother.

02:34:57.413 --> 02:34:59.833
Your son was the best I've fought.

02:35:03.086 --> 02:35:05.755
In my country, the funeral games
last for 12 days.

02:35:06.256 --> 02:35:08.383
It is the same in my country.

02:35:09.133 --> 02:35:11.302
Then the prince will have that honor.

02:35:12.178 --> 02:35:15.473
No Greek will attack Troy for 12 days.

02:35:21.604 --> 02:35:22.939
Briseis?

02:35:26.067 --> 02:35:28.444
I Thought you were dead.

02:35:39.122 --> 02:35:40.415
You are free.

02:35:56.848 --> 02:35:58.558
If I hurt you...

02:36:00.935 --> 02:36:03.146
...it's not what I wanted.

02:36:17.660 --> 02:36:18.953
Go.

02:36:19.370 --> 02:36:22.540
No one will stop you. You have my word.

02:36:23.333 --> 02:36:25.001
Come, my girl.

02:36:32.175 --> 02:36:35.887
You're a far better king than the one
leading this army.

02:36:52.403 --> 02:36:56.366
Achilles makes a secret pact, and I
have to honor it? What treason is this?

02:36:56.783 --> 02:37:00.787
Consorting with the enemy king.
Giving him 12 days of peace.

02:37:00.954 --> 02:37:03.081
Peace! Peace!

02:37:03.373 --> 02:37:06.084
Their prince is dead.
Their army is leaderless.

02:37:06.250 --> 02:37:07.877
This is the time to attack!

02:37:08.211 --> 02:37:12.382
Even with Hector gone, we have
no way to breach their walls.

02:37:12.966 --> 02:37:15.385
They can wait 10 years for us to leave.

02:37:16.636 --> 02:37:19.347
I Will smash their walls to the ground...

02:37:19.514 --> 02:37:22.100
...if it costs me 40,000 Greeks.

02:37:22.266 --> 02:37:24.894
Hear me, Zeus!

02:37:25.061 --> 02:37:28.773
I Will smash their walls to the ground.

02:39:16.089 --> 02:39:17.507
That's good.

02:39:17.882 --> 02:39:19.801
For my son back home.

02:39:46.661 --> 02:39:48.204
Well, Odysseus.

02:39:49.205 --> 02:39:53.876
You found a way to make the sheep
invite the wolves to dinner.

02:40:12.270 --> 02:40:15.982
Forgive me, Eudorus.
I should never have struck you.

02:40:18.276 --> 02:40:21.404
You've been a loyal friend all your life.

02:40:24.574 --> 02:40:27.243
I Hope I never disappoint you again.

02:40:27.577 --> 02:40:30.079
It's I who have been the disappointment.

02:40:33.583 --> 02:40:36.252
Rouse the men. You're taking them home.

02:40:38.588 --> 02:40:40.423
Aren't you coming with us?

02:40:41.215 --> 02:40:43.426
I Have my own battle to fight.

02:40:43.926 --> 02:40:45.595
Let me march beside you.

02:40:45.761 --> 02:40:49.599
No. I don't want our men
to be a part of this.

02:40:55.688 --> 02:40:57.523
It's a beautiful night.

02:40:58.191 --> 02:41:01.485
Go, Eudorus.
This is the last order I give you.

02:41:07.450 --> 02:41:10.620
Fighting for you has been
my life's honor, my lord.

02:41:24.300 --> 02:41:27.011
Open the gates!
Open the gates!

02:41:41.150 --> 02:41:42.818
Here.

02:42:09.178 --> 02:42:10.846
Plague.

02:42:11.514 --> 02:42:14.141
Don't go too close, my king.

02:42:14.892 --> 02:42:17.144
This is the will of the gods.

02:42:17.311 --> 02:42:19.230
They desecrated the temple of Apollo...

02:42:19.772 --> 02:42:22.275
...and Apollo desecrated their flesh.

02:42:22.441 --> 02:42:26.362
They thought they could come here
and sack our city in a day.

02:42:26.529 --> 02:42:30.366
Now look at them,
fleeing across the Aegean.

02:42:33.911 --> 02:42:35.705
What is this?

02:42:35.871 --> 02:42:40.584
An offering to Poseidon. The Greeks
are praying for a safe return home.

02:42:40.751 --> 02:42:43.629
I Hope the sea god spits in their offering.

02:42:43.796 --> 02:42:46.465
Lets them all drown
at the bottom of the sea.

02:42:46.632 --> 02:42:50.511
This is a gift. We should take it
to the temple of Poseidon.

02:42:51.554 --> 02:42:53.556
-I Think we should burn it.
-Burn it?

02:42:53.723 --> 02:42:55.558
My prince, it's a gift to the gods.

02:42:55.850 --> 02:42:58.060
The prince is right.

02:42:58.227 --> 02:43:01.772
I Would burn the whole of Greece
if I had a big enough torch.

02:43:01.939 --> 02:43:05.651
I Warn you, good men,
be careful what you insult.

02:43:06.235 --> 02:43:10.406
Our beloved Prince Hector
had sharp words for the gods...

02:43:10.573 --> 02:43:13.701
...and a day later
Achilles' sword cut him down.

02:43:13.868 --> 02:43:16.412
Father, burn it.

02:43:17.204 --> 02:43:20.124
Forgive me, my king,
I mean no disrespect...

02:43:20.291 --> 02:43:23.044
...but I don't want to see
any more sons of Troy...

02:43:23.210 --> 02:43:25.755
...incur the gods' wrath.

02:43:27.757 --> 02:43:31.469
I Will not watch another son die.

02:44:42.998 --> 02:44:44.542
Look at them.

02:44:46.377 --> 02:44:48.838
You'd think their prince had never died.

02:44:51.006 --> 02:44:53.092
You are their prince now.

02:44:53.843 --> 02:44:55.886
Make your brother proud.

02:50:48.489 --> 02:50:52.534
Let it burn! Let Troy burn!

02:50:52.701 --> 02:50:57.247
Burn it! For Menelaus! Burn it!

02:50:57.498 --> 02:51:02.336
Burn Troy! Burn Troy!

02:51:02.503 --> 02:51:06.131
I Promised you, brother!
I promised you!

02:51:06.298 --> 02:51:09.676
Burn it! Burn it for Menelaus!

02:51:54.221 --> 02:51:56.014
Briseis. Where is she?

02:51:56.181 --> 02:51:58.433
-Where?
-I don't know.

02:51:58.600 --> 02:52:00.435
Please. I have a son.

02:52:00.811 --> 02:52:03.272
Then get him out of Troy.

02:52:09.862 --> 02:52:11.196
Briseis!

02:52:15.367 --> 02:52:18.453
Paris! Andromache!

02:52:19.872 --> 02:52:21.707
Helen. We must go.

02:52:21.874 --> 02:52:23.876
-Where?
-I'll show you. Now. Hurry.

02:52:24.042 --> 02:52:25.460
Paris. Paris.

02:52:25.627 --> 02:52:28.338
It's a long way. Quick. We must go now.

02:52:28.505 --> 02:52:30.132
Briseis!

02:52:33.302 --> 02:52:35.095
Paris!

02:52:41.810 --> 02:52:43.145
It's a long way. Quick.

02:52:43.312 --> 02:52:45.647
Hurry. There's a tunnel.

02:52:47.858 --> 02:52:49.443
-Come.
-I stay.

02:52:49.610 --> 02:52:51.862
-No.
-My father will never abandon the city.

02:52:52.029 --> 02:52:53.113
I Can't leave him.

02:52:53.322 --> 02:52:56.825
The city is dead.
They're burning it to the ground.

02:52:58.869 --> 02:53:00.829
-What's your name?
-Aeneas.

02:53:00.996 --> 02:53:03.999
-Do you know how to use a sword?
-Yes.

02:53:04.166 --> 02:53:06.126
The sword of Troy.

02:53:06.293 --> 02:53:09.838
As long as it's in the hands of a Trojan,
our people have a future.

02:53:10.005 --> 02:53:12.549
Protect them, Aeneas.
Find them a new home.

02:53:12.799 --> 02:53:15.177
- I Will.
-Hurry. Quick.

02:53:15.344 --> 02:53:17.763
Paris, Paris, Briseis wasn't in her room.

02:53:17.930 --> 02:53:19.431
I'll find her.

02:53:21.850 --> 02:53:23.518
Go.

02:53:24.353 --> 02:53:26.063
-I'll stay with you.
-Go.

02:53:26.229 --> 02:53:27.439
Please don't leave me.

02:53:27.606 --> 02:53:29.775
-How could you love me if I ran now?
-Please.

02:53:29.942 --> 02:53:34.237
We will be together again, in this world
or the next. We will be together.

02:53:41.036 --> 02:53:42.663
Go.

02:53:46.249 --> 02:53:48.418
To the gate!

02:53:48.710 --> 02:53:50.420
Forward!

02:54:08.021 --> 02:54:09.564
Follow me!

02:54:11.817 --> 02:54:13.151
Into line!

02:54:15.153 --> 02:54:17.155
Soldiers of Troy...

02:54:17.447 --> 02:54:19.741
...you men are warriors!

02:54:19.908 --> 02:54:22.577
To lead you has been my honor!

02:54:24.037 --> 02:54:25.580
My prince!

02:54:27.290 --> 02:54:29.251
The boatman waits for us.

02:54:29.501 --> 02:54:33.880
I Say we make him wait a little longer!

02:54:56.319 --> 02:54:59.489
No one. Spare no one.

02:55:09.958 --> 02:55:11.334
Paris!

02:55:12.127 --> 02:55:14.087
Save yourself.

02:55:44.826 --> 02:55:46.119
Briseis!

02:56:09.059 --> 02:56:12.813
Beware, my friends.
I am a servant of the gods.

02:56:37.754 --> 02:56:40.674
Have you no honor?

02:56:40.841 --> 02:56:42.551
Have you no honor?

02:56:56.648 --> 02:56:59.734
I Wanted you alive, old man.

02:57:00.193 --> 02:57:03.113
I Wanted you to watch your city burn.

02:57:05.073 --> 02:57:06.867
Please.

02:57:08.243 --> 02:57:10.370
The children.

02:57:12.706 --> 02:57:16.710
Spare the innocents.

02:57:17.460 --> 02:57:19.337
Nobody's innocent.

02:57:20.130 --> 02:57:21.923
Nobody.

02:57:41.943 --> 02:57:44.446
Too late for prayer, priestess.

02:57:53.705 --> 02:57:57.334
I Almost lost this war
because of your little romance.

02:57:58.793 --> 02:58:03.173
I Want to taste what Achilles tasted.

02:58:18.146 --> 02:58:22.567
You'll be my slave in Mycenae.

02:58:22.734 --> 02:58:28.240
A Trojan priestess scrubbing my floors.

02:58:30.158 --> 02:58:31.493
And at night...

02:58:45.090 --> 02:58:46.758
Get up!

02:58:49.803 --> 02:58:51.680
Hold her.

02:59:00.063 --> 02:59:01.398
Come with me.

02:59:05.110 --> 02:59:06.653
No!

02:59:14.202 --> 02:59:17.330
Paris!

02:59:22.168 --> 02:59:23.712
No!

02:59:23.878 --> 02:59:25.422
Don't!

02:59:36.975 --> 02:59:39.894
Don't! Please!

02:59:45.400 --> 02:59:47.777
Paris! Don't!

03:00:20.685 --> 03:00:22.103
It's all right.

03:00:23.063 --> 03:00:24.939
It's all right.

03:00:48.046 --> 03:00:49.964
You gave me peace...

03:00:51.800 --> 03:00:53.843
...in a lifetime of war.

03:00:59.140 --> 03:01:00.475
Briseis, come.

03:01:04.813 --> 03:01:06.064
-No.

03:01:06.231 --> 03:01:07.482
You must.

03:01:07.649 --> 03:01:09.150
No.

03:01:09.484 --> 03:01:11.152
Troy is falling.

03:01:11.986 --> 03:01:14.364
-No.

03:01:14.531 --> 03:01:16.074
Begin anew.

03:01:17.659 --> 03:01:20.912
We must go. I know a way out.

03:01:27.710 --> 03:01:29.045
It's all right.

03:01:31.548 --> 03:01:33.258
Go.

03:01:40.932 --> 03:01:42.225
Go.

03:03:22.450 --> 03:03:24.077
Find peace...

03:03:25.036 --> 03:03:26.538
...my brother.

03:04:37.400 --> 03:04:41.946
If they ever tell my story, let them say...

03:04:42.113 --> 03:04:44.616
...I walked with giants.

03:04:45.283 --> 03:04:48.745
Men rise and fall like the winter wheat...

03:04:48.953 --> 03:04:51.539
...but these names will never die.

03:04:53.458 --> 03:04:56.961
Let them say I lived
in the time of Hector...

03:04:57.128 --> 03:04:59.380
...breaker of horses.

03:04:59.797 --> 03:05:01.716
Let them say...

03:05:01.883 --> 03:05:05.553
...I lived in the time of Achilles.

03:15:58.622 --> 03:16:00.624
[ENGLISH]
